{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>At that time.</b> At the end of forty days He was reconciled to me and said to me, <b>״Carve for yourself״</b>, and afterwards <b>״And you shall make yourself an ark״</b> — and I made the ark first, so that when I come down with the tablets in my hand, where would I put them? And this is not the ark that Bezalel made, for the Mishkan they were not occupied with until after the Day of Atonement, for when he descended from the mountain he commanded them concerning the work of the Mishkan, and Bezalel made the Mishkan first and afterwards the ark and the vessels. It follows that this was a different ark, and this is the one that went out with them to war, whereas the one Bezalel made did not go out to war — except in the days of Eli, and they were punished on its account and it was captured (Jerusalem Talmud, Shekalim 6)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:46:23.730267141Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}